blast radius Meaning: The scope of impact if something goes wrong — how far the “damage” spreads.

Single AWS Account:

If all workloads (prod, dev, test) are in one account, a compromised IAM user could affect everything.

👉 Large blast radius.

Multiple AWS Accounts:

If prod and dev are isolated in separate accounts, a compromise in dev doesn’t affect prod.

👉 Smaller blast radius.

Kubernetes/EKS:

If all workloads run in one namespace, a misconfigured RBAC role could expose all pods.

If workloads are isolated by namespace + network policies, the blast radius is reduced.

Isolation: Separate accounts, VPCs, namespaces, or node groups.

Least Privilege: IAM roles, RBAC, network policies.

Segmentation: Use service mesh policies, SCPs, firewalls.

